WEBVTT

00:00.270 --> 00:05.460
Perched above the yet oceanless ocean,
 there was once a dreamer.

00:05.460 --> 00:10.470
The dreamer dreamed of all 
of the things in the world.

00:10.890 --> 00:17.850
Day after day, doing nothing but dreaming, 
the dreamer eventually became a stone.

00:18.280 --> 00:22.240
That stone, known as the 
Mythical Star Stone, grew larger and larger

00:22.240 --> 00:25.480
and ultimately became an egg.

00:26.010 --> 00:31.370
An egg floating alone above 
the yet oceanless ocean.

02:12.210 --> 02:15.310
She was honestly kind of a 
weird girl, that Ichiki-san.

02:16.000 --> 02:17.790
Didn't you guys always pick on her?

02:17.790 --> 02:19.620
Hey, don't say that!

02:36.000 --> 02:38.090
What? Sayo killed herself?

02:38.660 --> 02:40.030
No, she didn't.

02:40.030 --> 02:43.740
I mean, she was saying, 
"I don't want to die" before it happened.

02:46.310 --> 02:47.930
Where did you hear that?

02:48.380 --> 02:50.200
Uh, I forget.

02:56.600 --> 02:59.200
Who was Sayo friends with anyway?

02:59.680 --> 03:00.720
Dunno.

03:05.720 --> 03:08.710
She was always staring up at the sky.

03:08.710 --> 03:11.050
Hey, kid! What do you think you're doing?

03:11.620 --> 03:14.380
Oh, man. Otori again?

03:15.100 --> 03:16.800
Why is he dressed like that?

03:31.140 --> 03:33.320
Stop right there, kid!

03:33.320 --> 03:36.030
Otori Sakko? You're at it again?

03:36.030 --> 03:37.200
Takechi-sensei...

03:37.460 --> 03:38.600
Sakko.

03:38.940 --> 03:39.900
Hey.

04:08.560 --> 04:13.940
<b>Specially Designated Private School
Enoshima Academy</b>

04:10.750 --> 04:16.280
In ancient times, humans worked up their 
courage to row out into the open sea.

04:13.070 --> 04:32.130
<b>Specially Designated Private School
Enoshima Academy</b>

04:13.860 --> 04:16.820
<b>Humans once took to the sea.</b>

04:16.280 --> 04:19.780
And today, we're headed for space.

04:17.400 --> 04:21.530
<b>Today, we take to space.</b>

04:22.520 --> 04:28.000
The Space Preservation Agency's Specially 
Designated Private School, Enoshima Academy.

04:22.870 --> 04:32.130
Inquire by Phone or Web

04:22.870 --> 04:32.130
<b>Accepting Applications Now</b>

04:22.870 --> 04:32.130
Enoshima Academy              <b>Search</b>

04:32.130 --> 04:36.880
<b>Today, you too can have a role in mythology.</b>

04:32.130 --> 04:36.880
Inquire by Phone or Web

04:32.130 --> 04:36.880
<b>Accepting Applications Now</b>

04:32.130 --> 04:36.880
Enoshima Academy

04:32.130 --> 04:36.880
Search

04:33.160 --> 04:36.310
Today, you too can have a role in mythology.

04:42.730 --> 04:47.730
Our thirteenth universe will perish as 
a result of humanity's own foolishness.

04:48.130 --> 04:52.090
Recurring disasters, pandemics, and wars.

04:52.090 --> 04:56.660
Each and every one of these 
is a part of their plan!

04:56.940 --> 04:59.190
<b>Judgment Day Is Near</b>

04:56.940 --> 04:59.190
<b>Stop the Thirteenth
Universe Annihilation Project</b>

04:56.940 --> 04:59.190
<b>Large-Scale Disasters</b>

04:56.940 --> 04:59.190
Pandemics

04:56.940 --> 04:59.190
<b>They Are All</b>

04:56.940 --> 04:59.190
<b>a Plot by the
World Government!</b>

05:08.250 --> 05:11.430
So now you should understand how, 
in strategic-form games,

05:11.430 --> 05:15.250
when all of the players have chosen a 
strategy that maximizes their payoff,

05:15.250 --> 05:18.340
they reach what is called 
a Nash equilibrium.

05:20.080 --> 05:22.330
In that situation, if any 
player alters their strategy,

05:22.330 --> 05:26.470
their payoff from that strategy will become 
less than it was before the change.

05:22.840 --> 05:24.930
Way out of line, Otori Sakko.

05:25.010 --> 05:27.100
At least wear your uniform at funerals

05:27.100 --> 05:28.970
I thought it was kinda cool though

05:27.170 --> 05:30.530
In other words, that means 
this is the optimal solution.

05:28.970 --> 05:30.980
Me, too

05:29.390 --> 05:30.980
Why do they always have
 carnations at funerals?

05:31.140 --> 05:33.310
Did Otori even know Ichiki? 
They're in different classes

05:31.270 --> 05:33.310
We covered the difference 
between a Nash equilibrium

05:33.060 --> 05:35.310
They were together since primary school

05:33.310 --> 05:34.780
and a Pareto optimum last time.

05:35.150 --> 05:37.480
Wait, so they were in the scout class?

05:37.360 --> 05:40.320
Momohime-sama from third-year was there too, right?
I hear the three of them were friends.

05:40.330 --> 05:44.250
Whoa, for real? Momohime-sama 
and Ichiki were both scouts?

05:44.250 --> 05:47.900
Crap. If I'd hung out with Ichiki, 
maybe she could've hooked me up.

05:47.900 --> 05:50.830
No way. She would've 
dropped you like a rock.

05:50.830 --> 05:54.800
Oh hey, Rimiya-kun, weren't you crying 
at Ichiki's funeral yesterday?

05:54.800 --> 05:56.250
Huh? Yeah.

05:56.250 --> 05:58.620
Were you that close?

05:58.620 --> 06:00.160
Hm...

06:00.600 --> 06:01.990
I never talked to her.

06:03.890 --> 06:07.120
Don't most people cry when 
their classmate dies?

06:07.830 --> 06:10.840
He's right. Are you guys totally heartless?

06:10.840 --> 06:13.720
Rimiya-kun isn't like you guys. 
He's actually kind.

06:13.720 --> 06:16.430
Huh? You guys didn't know 
her that well either.

06:16.430 --> 06:18.180
You sure can cry when you want to, though.

06:18.640 --> 06:19.280
Toshi.

06:19.510 --> 06:20.140
Huh?

06:20.140 --> 06:20.780
Let's go.

06:20.780 --> 06:22.010
Oh. Yeah.

06:35.340 --> 06:36.550
Momo, did you hear?

06:36.550 --> 06:39.530
They're about to announce the first 
selections for the advanced class!

06:39.530 --> 06:41.470
The Element class, right?

06:41.470 --> 06:43.200
So like grade school kids?

06:43.200 --> 06:45.040
Come on, that's "elementary."

06:45.040 --> 06:48.320
They're selecting students in 
third-year to form a new class.

06:48.320 --> 06:49.390
I don't get it.

06:49.390 --> 06:52.730
Our school is crazy, right? 
The classes are weird, too.

06:52.730 --> 06:55.460
Because it's a specially-designated 
Space Preservation Agency school.

06:55.940 --> 06:56.860
Did you hear?

06:56.860 --> 07:00.830
The Space Preservation Agency has a 
secret underground base in Enoshima!

07:00.830 --> 07:02.800
Yeah, that's just an urban legend.

07:02.800 --> 07:04.730
No! It's real, it's real!

07:04.730 --> 07:07.640
And I bet if you get chosen as an Element, 
you go straight into special training

07:07.640 --> 07:10.830
and get put on the fast track to 
the elite! How about that, Momo?

07:10.830 --> 07:12.440
I'm not really interested.

07:17.170 --> 07:20.400
Didn't Ichiki-san come to 
the library a lot, too?

07:20.400 --> 07:22.670
I only talked to her once.

07:22.670 --> 07:23.760
What did you talk about?

07:24.110 --> 07:27.830
Uh, I don't... really remember.

07:27.830 --> 07:29.790
I wasn't really interested.

07:29.790 --> 07:31.690
It was about past lives and stuff.

07:32.140 --> 07:32.940
Past lives?

07:32.940 --> 07:34.050
Yeah.

07:34.050 --> 07:39.980
Like we met each other in a past life 
and both had wings on our backs.

07:39.980 --> 07:42.400
I wonder if that's from a myth or something.

07:42.730 --> 07:46.640
Look, she used to read 
those books over there.

07:46.980 --> 07:49.790
Hold it, Otori! What are you doing here?

07:50.230 --> 07:51.830
Ouch, ouch.

07:51.830 --> 07:52.790
Shh!

07:52.180 --> 07:54.110
Where'd you go, Otori?

07:54.110 --> 07:56.650
I told you parkour isn't allowed at school!

07:56.650 --> 07:59.080
Not just school, in the whole city!

07:59.080 --> 08:01.790
Geez, I'm the one who's gonna get yelled at!

08:03.250 --> 08:04.280
Thank you.

08:04.280 --> 08:06.580
You're Otori-kun, right? From class 2?

08:06.580 --> 08:08.740
Yeah. You can call me Sakko.

08:09.030 --> 08:11.360
You're in class 1, right? Rimiya-kun and...

08:11.880 --> 08:13.170
I don't know your name.

08:13.170 --> 08:15.720
Hatano Toshi. Is parkour that fun?

08:15.980 --> 08:16.970
Not really.

08:17.690 --> 08:18.530
See you.

08:18.820 --> 08:20.380
Hey, wait up.

08:20.380 --> 08:21.420
What?

08:21.420 --> 08:23.570
You glared at me yesterday.

08:23.570 --> 08:25.610
Huh? Oh...

08:26.010 --> 08:27.540
Did I do something to you?

08:28.660 --> 08:31.260
Rimiya-kun, you don't have a heart, right?

08:32.270 --> 08:35.760
I saw you sometimes 'cause you're so popular.

08:35.760 --> 08:37.090
I can tell about stuff like that.

08:37.490 --> 08:38.450
Well, that's...

08:38.450 --> 08:41.070
Not that I care though. I don't either.

08:41.540 --> 08:45.040
But yesterday, it kind of pissed me off.

08:46.360 --> 08:49.490
He and Ichiki-san were in 
primary school together.

08:49.870 --> 08:50.750
Yeah.

08:52.250 --> 08:55.900
She never really took care of herself.

08:56.800 --> 08:59.220
She was always putting other people first.

08:59.220 --> 09:01.230
And she kept getting hurt because of it.

09:01.930 --> 09:04.260
It was so risky, I couldn't stand to watch.

09:04.260 --> 09:05.890
You were the one taking risks, Sakko.

09:05.200 --> 09:05.890
Oh!

09:08.870 --> 09:13.380
Sakko, you kept getting into dangerous 
situations and I kept stopping you.

09:13.380 --> 09:16.020
Sayo... What are you doing here?

09:16.680 --> 09:18.680
If we're going to fight mythical creatures,

09:18.680 --> 09:21.030
I thought I should get familiar with myths.

09:21.030 --> 09:22.510
Mythical creatures?

09:22.510 --> 09:26.310
Guys, let's do our best 
in the Element class.

09:26.310 --> 09:28.430
Element? You mean...

09:28.430 --> 09:30.420
There you are, Otori!

09:30.850 --> 09:34.430
I'm coming for you, so don't 
you move! Not even an inch!

09:36.100 --> 09:39.410
There you are. You guys are gonna 
freak out when you hear this.

09:41.580 --> 09:44.700
So they announced the members 
of the Element class?

09:44.700 --> 09:46.110
No way. Just three people?

09:46.110 --> 09:47.910
They might add more later, though.

09:47.910 --> 09:50.490
Rimiya-kun I can get, but Otori Sakko?

09:50.490 --> 09:53.950
Is Hatano that bookworm guy? 
But he always gets such bad grades.

09:54.260 --> 09:57.570
I was so sure you were gonna 
get chosen, Momohime.

09:58.190 --> 10:01.190
But I feel like there was one more.

10:01.190 --> 10:02.050
Huh?

10:13.600 --> 10:15.020
They're coming.

10:24.590 --> 10:27.350
I'm leading the Element class. 
My name is Munakata.

10:27.350 --> 10:30.600
Starting today, you'll be 
following a special curriculum

10:30.600 --> 10:33.910
designed to help you develop 
your abilities as Elements.

10:33.910 --> 10:36.890
It will be hard to manage this 
on top of your normal classes,

10:36.890 --> 10:38.020
so I hope you're ready.

10:38.020 --> 10:39.960
Doesn't the teacher see her?

10:39.960 --> 10:45.620
The first thing I need you to understand 
is that this program is top secret.

10:45.620 --> 10:49.130
You can't even tell your parents or 
siblings about your training here.

10:49.130 --> 10:50.040
Understood?

10:50.270 --> 10:51.200
Yes.

10:51.460 --> 10:52.500
Where's your answer?

10:52.800 --> 10:53.870
Yes!

11:01.020 --> 11:04.790
Now I'd like you to fight enemy soldiers, 
or mythical creatures,

11:04.790 --> 11:06.560
in this battle simulator.

11:06.560 --> 11:07.950
Mythical creatures?

11:08.300 --> 11:11.720
Sensei, why do you call the 
enemies mythical creatures?

11:11.720 --> 11:13.920
That's a good question, Ichiki-san.

11:13.920 --> 11:15.000
So she does see her.

11:15.000 --> 11:15.620
Yeah.

11:15.620 --> 11:18.440
We call them mythical creatures because 
they come from mythical space.

11:18.920 --> 11:20.960
Now get in the machines.

11:20.960 --> 11:22.130
Um...

11:21.620 --> 11:22.700
Um...

11:23.540 --> 11:24.800
Get a move on!

11:43.500 --> 11:45.460
So that's a mythical creature.

11:45.460 --> 11:47.360
Good luck, guys!

11:47.990 --> 11:50.080
Whoa!

11:47.990 --> 11:50.080
Whoa!

11:50.080 --> 11:51.510
Don't be afraid!

11:51.940 --> 11:53.310
Sakko, no!

11:54.130 --> 11:55.520
And don't be reckless!

11:55.520 --> 11:57.600
The Vector Machines amplify 
your emotional energy,

11:57.600 --> 11:59.730
your mana, and use it for power.

11:59.730 --> 12:02.970
The source of that mana is your 
strong desire to defeat the enemy.

12:02.970 --> 12:06.130
Mana? I can't keep up with 
all this complicated stuff!

12:06.130 --> 12:07.530
We just gotta do it!

12:07.530 --> 12:08.360
Okay!

12:18.460 --> 12:22.710
So that was one of the mythical creatures 
Ichiki-san was talking about.

12:22.710 --> 12:26.900
But how did she know about them 
before being chosen as an Element?

12:26.900 --> 12:30.390
And as soon as Element class 
ends, she disappears.

12:30.390 --> 12:34.070
She must have been chosen 
before the rest of us.

12:34.070 --> 12:35.620
Then for some reason,

12:35.620 --> 12:39.590
the teachers made it look like she 
died so she could start training.

12:40.000 --> 12:42.490
Yeah, I bet you're right.

12:45.550 --> 12:48.350
So why do you think it's us?

12:48.850 --> 12:49.650
Huh?

12:50.800 --> 12:52.890
Why do you think we were chosen?

12:53.310 --> 12:56.030
It's because of what you 
don't have. A heart.

12:56.700 --> 12:58.100
Where'd you come from?

13:01.080 --> 13:04.880
It was ripped out along 
with your wings that time.

13:04.880 --> 13:06.350
What time?

13:06.830 --> 13:09.130
12,000 years ago.

13:09.130 --> 13:12.120
Um, during the Jomon period?

13:12.840 --> 13:19.320
You must have realized that all of us are 
missing some part of our hearts, right?

13:19.890 --> 13:20.870
You mean...

13:20.870 --> 13:23.800
But if we're missing something,
 why were we chosen as Elements?

13:23.800 --> 13:27.970
Sensei said that the Vector 
Machines amplify your mana.

13:28.260 --> 13:31.450
Yeah, Munakata-sensei did 
say something about that.

13:31.990 --> 13:34.380
Mana, your emotional energy...

13:35.160 --> 13:38.550
But shouldn't we need to 
have hearts for that?

13:38.550 --> 13:41.820
The time has come! The time of destruction!

13:41.820 --> 13:45.680
They are plotting to destroy the universe!

13:45.680 --> 13:47.620
Listen! We'll all...

13:48.690 --> 13:53.290
Listen to me! Open your eyes, humankind!

13:58.700 --> 14:00.130
Out of all of them,

14:00.130 --> 14:03.700
why'd you have to choose kids 
with such poor mana balance?

14:03.700 --> 14:08.690
DEAVA deduced that this would be the 
optimal solution, Vice Principal.

14:08.690 --> 14:13.570
On top of that, we only have three 
Vector Machines that Elements can use!

14:13.570 --> 14:16.340
How are we supposed to protect 
the universe like this?

14:16.640 --> 14:20.270
If only we could have found those 
Mechanical Angels from the myths...

14:20.590 --> 14:21.990
What else can we do?

14:22.330 --> 14:26.640
We searched ruins all around the planet 
and still weren't able to find Aquarion.

14:26.640 --> 14:28.120
Principal!

14:28.120 --> 14:31.960
Not all of the predictions from 
the Naacal texts become reality.

14:31.960 --> 14:34.690
There is enough fluctuation range 
to allow for a different future.

14:34.690 --> 14:38.910
Is this more of that "universe's capability 
for revision" stuff, Saruta-kun?

14:39.180 --> 14:40.760
I don't know.

14:41.220 --> 14:46.080
Or maybe the me that does know will 
be revised and erased from history.

14:46.780 --> 14:49.920
So basically, things will 
go the way they go.

14:50.460 --> 14:52.520
That's going to be rough 
for these kids, though.

15:05.160 --> 15:07.320
Hey, Sakko. That's dangerous.

15:07.320 --> 15:08.340
Whoa.

15:08.970 --> 15:11.600
Momohime. Are you a ninja or something?

15:14.320 --> 15:19.560
Back in primary school, we always used to 
gaze at the stars like this. With Sayo.

15:19.560 --> 15:20.380
Yeah.

15:22.190 --> 15:23.820
I bet she liked them.

15:26.160 --> 15:27.110
The carnations.

15:27.610 --> 15:29.360
I'm surprised you remembered.

15:29.780 --> 15:32.620
I don't know why. 
It just popped into my head.

15:33.980 --> 15:35.480
Thank you.

15:35.480 --> 15:37.360
What are you thanking me for?

15:39.810 --> 15:42.290
Because Sayo was like my little sister.

15:43.790 --> 15:45.450
And you're my little brother!

15:47.810 --> 15:52.870
It sure is strange, about Sayo. 
It feels like she's still alive.

15:53.840 --> 15:56.340
I don't know. Seriously...

15:57.810 --> 15:59.060
is she?

15:59.640 --> 16:00.510
Huh?

16:18.960 --> 16:20.560
Sakko, you're going in too hot.

16:20.560 --> 16:22.170
So what? Keep up.

16:22.170 --> 16:25.320
Mythical creatures travel here 
through a crack in space.

16:25.320 --> 16:27.160
It's best if you can defeat them here,

16:27.160 --> 16:29.100
but we still win if you only send them back.

16:29.100 --> 16:31.050
Right, but how?

16:31.860 --> 16:33.400
Here it comes!

16:57.620 --> 16:58.830
Is that...

16:59.990 --> 17:01.210
a crack?

17:01.700 --> 17:03.120
This is bad news!

17:07.140 --> 17:10.830
<i>Munakata-sensei, a crack has appeared.</i>

17:10.830 --> 17:11.750
Huh?

17:12.140 --> 17:16.360
DEAVA is telling us to send 
those kids in to fight.

17:17.730 --> 17:20.360
The enemy is coming.

17:20.670 --> 17:23.210
<i>But they're still in training!</i>

17:23.570 --> 17:26.570
If they don't scramble now, 
the universe will collapse!

17:26.570 --> 17:28.320
That's the logical consequence 
in game theory.

17:32.000 --> 17:34.860
So they're finally here. 
Prepare to intercept!

17:34.860 --> 17:37.040
But this is still too soon!

17:48.080 --> 17:50.090
Going into actual combat already?

17:50.090 --> 17:51.290
Sensei...

17:51.630 --> 17:55.080
<i>Do it while the Preservation Agency 
drones are intercepting! Hurry!</i>

17:55.640 --> 17:59.060
Understood. Teleport them now.

17:59.060 --> 18:00.270
Teleport?

18:04.230 --> 18:06.730
Vector Siegel, prepare for launch.

18:09.260 --> 18:11.920
All storage units, engage safety barriers.

18:12.450 --> 18:14.200
Turret activating.

18:14.780 --> 18:17.910
Bridge catapult, activate launch sequence.

18:18.370 --> 18:20.740
Release bridge and raise lifts.

18:21.230 --> 18:25.260
For your safety, entering 
the area is now prohibited.

18:25.260 --> 18:28.940
Civilians should take 
shelter immediately.

18:29.470 --> 18:31.970
Electromagnetic catapult cover opened.

18:32.450 --> 18:36.310
Main shaft opened. Elevated turrets raising.

18:36.310 --> 18:38.580
Vector magnetically coupled with shuttle.

18:39.140 --> 18:42.730
Launch path all green. Propulsion engaged.

18:44.040 --> 18:46.400
Vector Siegel, launching.

18:47.190 --> 18:50.060
Yacht harbor, launch sequence initiated.

18:51.180 --> 18:54.190
Raising electromagnetic catapult.
 Prepare for launch.

18:54.500 --> 18:58.620
Turret activating. Vector magnetically 
coupled with shuttle.

18:58.620 --> 19:01.090
Successfully moved to launch position.

19:01.090 --> 19:04.230
Electromagnetic catapult bay doors opening.

19:04.230 --> 19:07.490
Rails extended. Launch path all green.

19:07.950 --> 19:08.950
Propulsion engaged.

19:10.630 --> 19:13.000
Vector Feoh, launching.

19:18.420 --> 19:22.520
Iwaya cave, launch sequence 
initiated. Bay doors opened.

19:22.520 --> 19:25.890
Vector magnetically coupled with 
shuttle. Propulsion engaged.

19:26.260 --> 19:28.530
Vector Tir, launching.

19:32.520 --> 19:33.620
Huh? What?

19:34.820 --> 19:37.400
It felt like my body just flew somewhere.

19:37.400 --> 19:39.010
Where are we?

19:41.790 --> 19:44.350
Um, this feels strangely real.

19:44.350 --> 19:46.400
<i>Correct, Tsukishiro Rimiya-kun.</i>

19:46.400 --> 19:48.660
<i>This is not training. This is reality.</i>

19:48.660 --> 19:50.370
Huh? Saruta-sensei?

19:50.370 --> 19:52.120
Reality?!

19:52.120 --> 19:53.180
There's something here!

19:53.180 --> 19:56.080
That is our enemy's weapon of 
invasion, a mythical creature.

19:56.080 --> 19:58.130
If you want to survive, destroy it!

19:58.130 --> 19:58.970
Huh?

20:01.340 --> 20:03.470
Ah! It's coming this way!

20:04.560 --> 20:07.900
All ships, coordinate your attacks. 
Remember your training!

20:08.370 --> 20:10.400
I'll distract it, so attack from behind!

20:10.400 --> 20:11.150
Okay.

20:11.150 --> 20:12.280
You're already on it?!

20:18.250 --> 20:21.920
Real combat doesn't faze him at all.

20:22.870 --> 20:24.690
That's good. Again!

20:35.180 --> 20:36.270
This is bad.

20:36.760 --> 20:38.190
The mana is becoming unstable!

20:53.420 --> 20:54.830
It's over.

21:04.310 --> 21:05.190
Guys!

21:07.880 --> 21:08.690
Huh?

21:14.180 --> 21:15.380
Ouch!

21:15.380 --> 21:18.610
Try to remember what it 
was like to have wings.

21:20.940 --> 21:22.620
What is this?

21:28.620 --> 21:30.060
Aquarion.

21:32.800 --> 21:35.450
Go... Aquarion!

21:36.770 --> 21:39.290
What's happening? I feel sick.

21:39.290 --> 21:41.360
Is this both of your...

21:41.690 --> 21:46.230
Yeah, I can feel it coming from you guys!

21:53.260 --> 21:55.090
Could that possibly be...

21:56.260 --> 21:59.040
When the sun, the moon, 
and Mars come into alignment,

21:59.660 --> 22:02.050
the melody of a new union 
begins to resonate.

22:04.320 --> 22:07.470
Mechanical Angel Aquarion!
